<article class="env-definition" id="00RN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00RN">Definition <span data-tag="00RN">10.131.1</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : R \to S$ be a ring map and let $M$ be an $S$-module. A <em>derivation</em>, or more precisely an <em>$R$-derivation</em> into $M$ is a map $D : S \to M$ which is additive, annihilates elements of $\varphi (R)$, and satisfies the <em>Leibniz rule</em>: $D(ab) = aD(b) + bD(a)$. </p>
</article>